{"ref":"BDB, צֹר²","hw":"צֹר²","html":"† II. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">צֹר</span></big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>id.</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">צ׳</span> used as knife <a data-ref=\"Exodus 4:25\" href=\"/Exodus.4.25\">Ex 4:25</a>; in comp., <span dir=\"rtl\">כְּשָׁמִיר חָזָק מִצּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 3:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.3.9\">Ez 3:9</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">חַרְבוֹת צֻרִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 5:2\" href=\"/Joshua.5.2\">Jos 5:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 5:3\" href=\"/Joshua.5.3\">3</a> <em>knives of flint</em>.—<span dir=\"rtl\">צוּר חַרְבּוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 89:44\" href=\"/Psalms.89.44\">ψ 89:44</a> is dub., <span dir=\"rtl\">צ׳</span> usually taken as = <span dir=\"rtl\">צֹר</span>, and then either <em>flint of his sword</em> (i.e. sword sharp as flint, Bae), or <em>edge</em> (like flint) <em>of his sword</em> (most); We leaves untransl. <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 2:16\" href=\"/II_Samuel.2.16\">2 S 2:16</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">חֶלְקַת הַצֻּרִים</span> v. i. <a data-ref=\"BDB, חֶלְקָה²\" href=\"/BDB,_חֶלְקָה²\", dir=\"rtl\">חֶלְקָה</a>.—<a data-ref=\"Job 22:24\" href=\"/Job.22.24\">Jb 22:24</a> v. i. <a data-ref=\"BDB, צוּר⁴\" href=\"/BDB,_צוּר⁴\", dir=\"rtl\">צוּר</a> sub V. <a data-ref=\"BDB, צור²\" href=\"/BDB,_צור²\", dir=\"rtl\">צור</a>. i. <a data-ref=\"BDB, צֹר\" href=\"/BDB,_צֹר\", dir=\"rtl\">צֹר</a> v. p. 862.","next":"BDB, צְרוֹר²","prev":"BDB, צַר⁵"}